{
 "schema": "v8.delta/2",
 "phase": "v8 Phase 5: economic exposure safety - Extended category Crypto becomes wrapper evidence only, Lighter token-list asset_type RWA becomes tradfi evidence, an exposure seen only through a failed exposure check is not verified by the ticker list (v8.identity/3)",
 "base": {
  "sha": "3288b1587563045558ea42dec70301e61dc95a9e",
  "tree": "d56ef755e23827ba8e2910a6d69d4b6f61090c2f",
  "golden": "tests/fixtures/v8/legacy_parity_golden_phase4.json",
  "golden_note": "main 3288b15 (Phase 4 merged, PR #15) on the fixture: the Phase 4 branch golden. The Phase 5 fixture adds only fields the base code never reads (Extended subCategory) and a URL it never requests (the Lighter token list), so the base reproduces it unchanged"
 },
 "head_golden": "tests/fixtures/v8/legacy_parity_golden_phase5.json",
 "counterfactual_projection": "exclude_without_execution_identity",
 "rules": {
  "EXTENDED_CRYPTO_WRAPPER_ONLY": "v8.identity/3: Extended category 'Crypto' describes the instrument wrapper, not the economic exposure (Extended files tokenized gold PAXG and XAUT under it), so it is wrapper evidence only - recorded and traced, never crypto evidence. A coin whose only crypto authority was that label (no known-crypto ticker, no other evidence) is UNVERIFIED (WRAPPER_ONLY_NO_ECONOMIC_EVIDENCE): it stays in the universe (discovery) and loses crypto execution identity.",
  "LIGHTER_TOKENLIST_RWA_TRADFI": "v8.identity/3: a Lighter market whose entry in Lighter's token list (/api/v1/tokenlist, asset_type documented as CRYPTO | RWA; Lighter's RWAs are commodities, equities and fixed income) has asset_type RWA carries tradfi evidence on its own contract (VENUE_ASSET_TYPE:RWA), within its own price-coherent exposure only. CRYPTO is no evidence.",
  "WRAPPER_NOT_COUNTED_AS_CRYPTO": "A DEX's count of crypto markets counts only markets admitted with crypto execution identity: the markets of a coin verified by Extended's Crypto wrapper alone are no longer counted.",
  "UNVERIFIED_PRICE_CHECK_NOTE": "A coin with no crypto exposure keeps the Phase 2 record of its UNVERIFIED exposures (v8.identity rule 5), whose legacy price check drops a venue far from the most traded market and notes it. PRLX's two exposures are both UNVERIFIED since /3, so the note Phase 3 stopped emitting (UNVERIFIED_EXPOSURE_NOT_MERGED, when PRLX was verified crypto) is emitted again; the Lighter market stays out of the record.",
  "UNVERIFIED_LISTED_SEPARATELY": "The radar publishes identity-unverified coins in coverage.unverified, not among the non-crypto (tradfi) exclusions in coverage.tradfi: unknown is not tradfi. The counterfactual hands every coin without crypto execution identity to the base code as tradfi (its only exclusion); HEAD lists the unverified ones apart.",
  "IDENTITY_VERSION_BUMP": "Entry-time identity provenance of a paper trade opened in this run records the identity version of the authority that allowed it: v8.identity/3. Written once; a trade opened under v8.identity/2 keeps its proof and stays qualified (no hindsight). Every other trade value is unchanged."
 },
